  "conclusion": "Fathers on the high-fat diet became obese and insulin resistant (HOMA-IR 2.29 vs 0.88, p_welch = 1.50e-05). Their daughters - despite eating a control diet and having normal body weight (12-wk weight p = 0.47) - showed halved glucose-stimulated insulin secretion (insulinogenic index 38.7 vs 86.8, diff +48.1, 95% bootstrap CI [30.6, 65.0], p_rand = 0.0004) and a higher 6-week glucose peak (13.6 vs 12.3 mM, p_rand = 0.023). Expression changes were broad: 56/77 altered islet genes down-regulated (z = 3.99, p = 6.6e-05). Paternal pre-conception diet measurably reprograms daughters' metabolic health - experiences of parents do affect future children."
}
